Create an `Adapter` class that implements the `Logger` interface and contains an instance of `LegacyLogger`. Its `info(String message)` method would call `legacyLogger.logMessage(message)`. 
```java
interface Logger { void info(String message); }
class LegacyLogger { void logMessage(String msg) { /* ... */ } }
class LegacyLoggerAdapter implements Logger {
    private LegacyLogger legacyLogger;
    public LegacyLoggerAdapter(LegacyLogger ll) { this.legacyLogger = ll; }
    @Override public void info(String message) { legacyLogger.logMessage(message); }
}
```
